# Pi Sandbox Workflows

Canonical project Brain for `/Users/joel/Code/joelhooks/pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows`.

This note was moved from the top-level `joelhooks/.brain/projects/ephemeral-pi-sandboxes.svx` so future design/prototype receipts live with the repo that owns the work.

## Decision

The browser terminal Cloudflare prototype proved that Pi can run in a Cloudflare Sandbox with ChatGPT/Codex subscription OAuth seeded through `~/.pi/agent/auth.json`, but the desired product shape is **contextual sandboxes for bounded runs**, not a persistent browser TUI.

Accepted identity boundary: **context capsule keyed by the external work item/thread**, not by sandbox ID. Sandbox IDs are replaceable compute handles; the capsule owns durable state.

## App spine decisions — 2026-06-08

Accepted production-domain boundary:

- The production surface is **the app**, not `v0`, `vzero`, or a launch-phase name. Launch-phase labels belong in Brain/planning notes, not code/domain names.
- Schema/TypeScript is a hard architecture boundary: Zod owns runtime artifact contracts, TypeScript types are inferred from Zod, and D1 row schemas stay adapter-local. Do not create parallel hand-written domain interfaces that can drift from schemas.
- Use DDD language from `joelclaw.com/api/docs`: a bounded context with ubiquitous language. Core domain terms are actor, context capsule, package, pinned package, dynamic workflow blueprint, generated XState workflow machine, generated harness, dynamic workflow plan, safety envelope, agent lane, capability, lease, receipt, and review gate.
- Configured familiar identity is data. A configured name such as ShitRat can appear in seed data, package metadata, fixtures, or operator config, but must not become a domain type, table name, route name, or hardcoded core concept.
- Ports and adapters are first-class: the application depends on ports for context capsules, package registry, Artifact store, dynamic workflow planner, agent lanes, capability lease broker, Discord messages, and review gates.
- Package is the top-level saved primitive. Context packs, workflow packs, tool packs, support packs, adapters, org kernels, and personal kernels are package categories rooted at `package.json`.
- D1 indexes package metadata and entitlements; D1 is not the package source of truth.
- Capability leasing is in the first app slice. Dry-run still requests and receives a lease; dry-run only relaxes review/secret material requirements.
- Dynamic workflows are in the first app slice. A stochastic planner generates/selects a blueprint with a `workflow.xstate-machine.v1` generated XState machine and a `workflow.dynamic-plan.v1` plan. The app pins `workflows/machine.config.json` and inspectable `workflows/machine.ts` first, then writes `run/plan.json` with machine refs/hashes. Execution drives the generated XState actor under the fixed safety envelope.
- Production progress: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-artifacts-store.ts` now provisions per-run Cloudflare Artifacts repos and exposes a Git-backed `ArtifactStoreContract` for plan-phase writes and commit-targeted lane reads. `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-sandbox-agent-lanes.ts` contains a Cloudflare Sandbox Pi lane runtime adapter scaffold. It requires an HTTPS Artifacts remote, short-lived Artifacts token, and leased Pi auth material backed by redacted `AgentAuthLease` metadata; writes prompt/output/transcript/receipt artifacts in the sandbox; pushes the lane branch; destroys the sandbox; and returns a schema-validated `AgentLaneReceipt` with `realAgent: true`, `artifactCommitSha`, `authLease`, and `sandboxAccounting` cleanup/duration metadata. Production-mode `pi-*` lane receipts are invalid without auth-lease metadata. `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-agent-lane-adapters.ts` wraps that runtime for planner, worker, and verifier lane ports. The planner lane strict output is `PlannerLaneBlueprintDocument` (`machine`, `harness`, `plan`, `verificationContract`); the adapter, not the planner, attaches real planner lane evidence from prompt/transcript/output receipts.
- Lane admission progress: `src/app/application/admitted-agent-lane-runtime.ts` wraps any real `AgentLaneRuntimePort` with `AgentLaneAdmissionControllerContract`, refuses deferred/already-completed lanes, and releases admitted slots as completed/failed with optional `artifactCommitSha`. `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-capsule-supervisor.ts` adds a Durable Object supervisor/client implementing context capsule resolution, event append, bounded lane admission, and lane release receipts keyed by external `workItemId`. This moves bounded hot concurrency from prototype lore into app ports/adapters.
- Package registry progress: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-package-registry.ts` implements `PackageRegistryActorContract` with D1 as package/entitlement index and Artifacts `package.json` as source truth. Discovery reads entitled manifests from Artifacts. Pinning requires mount entitlement, verifies D1 row fields plus optional manifest hash against the manifest, and emits `PinnedPackage` hashes from the manifest artifact. Stale/mismatched rows block as `stale_package`.
- Front-door composition progress: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-workflow-front-door.ts` is the production-intended `POST /runs` composition root. It provisions the per-run Artifacts repo, resolves the DO capsule/admission client, wraps the Cloudflare Sandbox Pi runtime with admission, wires real planner/worker/verifier adapters, wires the plan-selected deterministic verifier adapter, wires the D1 + Artifacts package registry, constructs the run-scoped D1 + Artifacts capability lease broker when no test broker is injected, and constructs `WorkflowApp` in production mode. `tests/integration/cloudflare-workflow-front-door.test.ts` drives the composition with an injected real-lane-shaped runtime and proves planner, worker, and verifier all pass through admission and return `pi-agent-cli` receipts.
- Worker route progress: `src/app/worker.ts` now exports the Worker handler, Sandbox class, and capsule Durable Object class. `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-worker-route.ts` validates `POST /runs` requests before delegating to the front-door contract, serves the redacted `GET /runs/:runId/events` observer route from D1 event projections, and serves `GET /runs/:runId/debugger` as a typed `workflow.debugger-attach.v1` read-only attach descriptor over the same event receipts. The event route supports JSON snapshot, SSE replay, bounded live-tail SSE, and WebSocket live observation with `after` / `Last-Event-ID` resume support plus typed `workflow.event-tail-control.v1` close events. `wrangler.jsonc`, `worker-configuration.d.ts`, root `Dockerfile`, `migrations/0001_workflow_app_d1.sql`, `migrations/0002_workflow_telemetry_logs.sql`, and `migrations/0003_workflow_events.sql` define the deployable Cloudflare binding/type surface without hand-written `Env`; the Pi model is an operator-supplied runtime binding, not a checked-in guessed model string, and `PI_AUTH_SECRET_REF` names the lease source separately from secret material. Latest live app deploy receipt: Worker `https://pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows.joelhooks.workers.dev`, version `9ae36391-4b24-4166-9b5b-87ad7fbf5feb`, D1 database `72ab80e4-600d-4dd8-b581-8560eff16967`, Analytics Engine dataset `pi_cloudflare_sandbox_workflows_telemetry`.
- Package Artifacts reader progress: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-package-artifacts-reader.ts` resolves concrete package manifest refs shaped as `artifact://cloudflare-artifacts/<repo-name>/<path>` and defaults to `package.json`. Logical package refs such as `artifact://packages/...` stay package-domain data and are not coerced into infrastructure repo names.
- Package seed progress: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-package-seeder.ts` and package admin routes now create or update package Artifacts repos, write package manifests, and mirror package/entitlement rows into D1 behind `WORKFLOW_APP_ADMIN_TOKEN`. Core package seed defaults include `badass-courses/claw-kernel`, `joelhooks/configured-familiar-kernel`, and `workflow/research-review-discord`; installed workflow cartridges contribute their own package seed templates through `src/cartridges/cloudflare-workflow-cartridges.ts`. The Dream cartridge owns `workflow/dream-memory-fabric` package seed data in `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/package-seed.ts`, exports `dream-transcript-review-source-profile`, and exports twelve workflow nodes: `joelclaw.dream.source-inventory`, `joelclaw.dream.source-health`, `joelclaw.dream.backfill-plan`, `joelclaw.dream.backfill-run`, `joelclaw.dream.capture-run`, `joelclaw.dream.capture-artifact`, `joelclaw.dream.signals`, `joelclaw.dream.memory-search`, `joelclaw.dream.hydrate`, `joelclaw.dream.correlate`, `joelclaw.dream.refinement-proposals`, and `joelclaw.dream.hitl-report`. The Worker package seed route combines core defaults with installed cartridge package seeds. Dream package reseed receipt `.wrangler/workflow-app/latest-dream-package-reseed-receipt.json` completed at `2026-06-10T05:50:25.488Z`, deployed Worker version `ce3a3eec-a6c1-429c-8f4d-8c97e88928b9`, and seeded `workflow/dream-memory-fabric` with manifest hash `b36403a390d8a5f117d7ce302c0dff0579064e925999ef8767cf6680a3c0df1b` at seed commit `b1b5a8a7a0fc5b67c4d70fe31892f1e242f53039`. The setup rotated `WORKFLOW_APP_ADMIN_TOKEN` through the deploy secrets file and did not provision `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_TOKEN` or inject any Dream relay URL.
- Dream live preflight progress: `workflow.live-preflight.v1` is the typed readiness receipt for Cloudflare-backed workflow cartridges. `scripts/workflow-app-dream-preflight.ts` verifies env/config gates, remote Cloudflare D1 package rows, remote Worker secret names, generated-artifact proof requirements, side-effect lease prerequisites, required machine coverage, required source-family coverage, and the authenticated Dream relay `/healthz` readiness receipt before a Dream run can claim live readiness. Latest receipt `.wrangler/workflow-app/dream-preflight/latest-dream-preflight.json`, generated `2026-06-10T06:42:35.895Z`, confirms the remote Dream package artifact ref and manifest hash match the current cartridge. Remote Worker secrets include `WORKFLOW_APP_ADMIN_TOKEN`, `PI_AUTH_JSON_B64`, `WORKFLOW_APP_MODEL`, `DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, and `WZRRD_API_TOKEN`; `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_TOKEN` is still missing. Local proof `run:dream-relay-local-proof:20260610T064219761Z` captures required runtimes Pi/Codex/Claude/Cloudflare, machine coverage for `blaine`, `panda`, `flagg`, and Cloudflare, source families `agent-transcripts`, `brain`, `cloudflare-runs`, `docs-pdf-brain`, and `repo-outputs`, mined `dream.signals.v1` receipts, run/artifact capture receipts, 12 hydrated redacted receipts, 48 correlation edges, and 35 correlation nodes. Latest live run request `run-live-dream-memory-fabric-20260610T064233737Z-4441393c` wrote `.wrangler/workflow-app/dream-runs/run-live-dream-memory-fabric-20260610T064233737Z-4441393c-receipt.json` with `submit.attempted=false`. AIHero support/comms/CRM roots were moved out of the active Dream relay config and saved as a separate workflow-candidate source pack. Remaining live gates are `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_BASE_URL`, `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_TOKEN`, Worker deploy config or signoff-gated deploy-time injection for `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_BASE_URL`, authenticated relay `/healthz`, and exact owner sign-off before any new relay exposure.
- Dream relay deploy gate progress: `scripts/workflow-app-deploy-and-seed.mjs` can now inject `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_BASE_URL`, `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_SECRET_REF`, and `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_USER_AGENT` into a temporary generated Wrangler config for deployment, but only when `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_BASE_URL` is HTTPS and the deploy call carries the exact sign-off phrase through `--dream-relay-approval-signoff`, `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_APPROVAL_SIGNOFF`, or `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_PROVISIONING_SIGNOFF`. The generated config is deleted after deploy, the relay URL/secret ref are redacted from deploy stdout/stderr receipts, and the live preflight only accepts deploy-time URL injection when the deploy harness support is present. Safety proof `.wrangler/workflow-app/dream-relay/signoff-gate-deploy-proof.json` at `2026-06-10T04:53:11.718Z` set `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_BASE_URL` without sign-off; the harness failed before `wrangler deploy` with `workerUrl=null`.
- Dream memory relay contract progress: `dream.memory-relay.request.v1`, `dream.memory-relay.response.v1`, and `dream.memory-relay.endpoint-catalog.v1` now define the trusted relay boundary for Cloudflare Dream nodes. The full catalog covers inventory, search, signals, hydration, correlation, backfill plan/run, source health, and capture run/artifact endpoints. Requests carry actor/scope/source-family/purpose/budget/time-window/redaction/idempotency/lease/trace metadata; responses carry lease receipts, missing sources, freshness, inventory refs, follow-up links, and typed Dream documents. Existing Cloudflare relay calls now use this envelope for inventory/source-health/backfill-plan instead of posting raw node inputs.
- Dream relay lease proof progress: `workflow.execution-proof.v1` now records generic `workflowNodeOutputRefs`, and relay-backed Dream cartridge nodes write `dream/relay-lease-receipts/<stepId>.json` sidecars when the trusted relay returns a used `dream.memory-relay` lease receipt. `dream.generated-workflow-proof.v1` records `relayLeaseReceiptRefs` and fails Cloudflare-status Dream proof on `execution:relay-lease-sidecars` unless every relay-backed generated step emitted a matching sidecar. Local integration can still verify the generated plan/machine/harness chain, but it stays `not-proven-local-integration` and has zero relay sidecars.
- Trusted relay server progress: `src/app/infrastructure/trusted-dream-memory-relay-server.ts` now validates the Dream relay HTTP boundary server-side. It checks method, route, bearer auth, request envelope, operation/path match, operation support, and operation-specific payloads before delegating to generic `DreamMemoryFabricPort` / `DreamMemoryRetrievalPort` contracts. Core app owns the relay host contract; installed workflow cartridges own concrete Dream source adapters.
- Dream cartridge boundary correction: the trusted local Dream memory fabric/retrieval/HTTP relay implementation moved out of `src/app/infrastructure` and into `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/`. `src/app/index.ts` no longer exports the local Dream relay or local filesystem adapters. Dream remains a loaded workflow cartridge/package capability; the runner must not grow Dream-specific if/else/switch branches. The installed-cartridge combiner now composes multiple workflow-node adapter factories generically, treating `adapter_unavailable` as "try the next cartridge" while preserving real blockers such as `stale_package`.
- Dynamic runtime boundary correction: the Dream cartridge now owns deterministic package metadata and a `dream.source-profile.v1` transcript-review profile, but it must not own the run-specific workflow runtime. `scripts/workflow-app-dream-run.ts` no longer prompts for a fixed "Required Dream node order"; it gives the planner the source profile and node palette, then requires generated XState/harness/verifier proof that the selected dynamic machine produced the required effects and receipts. `dream.generated-workflow-proof.v1` records the source-profile fingerprint and fails `plan:source-profile-bound` when the generated plan does not cite the installed profile or the pinned package lacks the matching source-profile export. The old `plan:all-dream-nodes` check was replaced by `plan:profile-effect-coverage`, and the proof now records `effectCoverage.requiredEffects` plus `effectCoverage.coveredEffects`; a regression proves an `11`-step generated plan can verify when one step explicitly covers multiple Dream effects. This proves profile/effect binding without turning Dream into a canned phase list.
- Dream source-pack contract progress: `dream.source-profile.v1` now has typed `sourcePacks` with surfaces, source families, scope, privacy tier, required capability kinds, and selection policy. The installed transcript-review profile advertises `source-pack:joelhooks:work-graph` as an optional leased pack for GitHub/Linear/Slack/org-project-graph correlation and keeps `source-pack:badass-courses:aihero-support-sweep` as a separate-workflow candidate. `scripts/workflow-app-dream-run.ts` includes these packs in planner instructions, and `dream.generated-workflow-proof.v1` includes them in the source-profile fingerprint. Required Dream readiness still stays on `agent-transcripts`, `brain`, `cloudflare-runs`, `docs-pdf-brain`, and `repo-outputs`; optional support/comms/org surfaces do not clear or block live readiness unless selected under scoped leases.
- Dream source-pack disposition proof progress: generated Dream plans must now declare `dreamSourcePackDispositions` for every advertised source pack. `dream.generated-workflow-proof.v1` records disposition count, expected/missing/unexpected pack ids, and per-pack status (`selected-by-default`, `selected-with-lease`, `skipped-missing-lease`, or `separate-workflow-candidate`), and fails `plan:source-pack-disposition` if optional packs lack an explicit lease/skipped decision or separate-workflow packs are folded into transcript-review readiness. Integration coverage strips dispositions from an otherwise valid Dream plan to prove rejection.
- Dream horizon-coverage proof progress: `dream.generated-workflow-proof.v1` now records `horizonCoverage.requiredHorizons` and `horizonCoverage.coveredHorizons`, and fails `plan:horizon-coverage` when generated Dream retrieval/signal steps do not declare `dreamCoverageHorizons` for the source profile. `scripts/workflow-app-dream-run.ts` now tells the planner to declare the five required horizons, and integration coverage strips those declarations from an otherwise valid Dream plan to prove the verifier rejects recent-only retrieval.
- Dream runtime/source coverage proof progress: `dream.generated-workflow-proof.v1` now records `runtimeSourceCoverage` for required runtimes, source families, and machine ids from the installed source profile, and fails `plan:runtime-source-coverage` when a generated source-inventory step does not bind inventory to Pi/Codex/Claude/Cloudflare plus `blaine`/`panda`/`flagg`/Cloudflare. Integration coverage strips `requiredMachineIds` from an otherwise valid generated inventory step to prove the verifier rejects profile name-dropping without source coverage binding.
- Trusted local Dream memory fabric progress: `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/trusted-local-memory-fabric.ts` implements the first real relay-side `DreamMemoryFabricPort` for local authority roots. It inventories configured Pi/Codex/Claude/Cloudflare/Brain-style roots with redacted locators, hashes raw paths, counts files, checks derived QMD/Typesense/view/vector/SQLite indexes, emits source health, and plans recovery-only backfills/capture fixes without leaking raw private paths to Cloudflare. This is an installable Dream cartridge adapter, not runner logic.
- Trusted local Dream relay HTTP progress: `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/trusted-local-relay-http.ts`, `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/trusted-local-memory-retrieval.ts`, and `scripts/trusted-local-dream-memory-relay.ts` compose the trusted relay handler plus local memory-fabric/retrieval/correlation/capture adapters into a runnable Node HTTP endpoint. `pnpm app:dream:relay` starts from `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_SOURCE_ROOTS_JSON` and `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_TOKEN`; `/healthz` is bearer-authenticated and returns a redacted `trusted.dream-memory-relay.readiness.v1` receipt with endpoint catalog and source config summaries, not raw paths or token material. The relay now exposes inventory/source-health/backfill-plan/backfill-run/capture-run/capture-artifact/signals/search/hydrate/correlate when the cartridge is installed locally.
- Dream retrieval/correlation cartridge progress: generated Dream workflows can now invoke `joelclaw.dream.memory-search`, `joelclaw.dream.hydrate`, and `joelclaw.dream.correlate` as package-backed `workflow.node.invoke` states. The Cloudflare relay client implements `DreamMemoryFabricPort`, `DreamMemoryRetrievalPort`, and `DreamMemoryCorrelationPort`; the Worker route wires the same leased relay adapter into those ports, and the artifact-backed cartridge adapter verifies the package export before each search/hydration/correlation node runs. This enables T-shaped Dream retrieval plus an explicit correlation graph in the generated workflow language; it still needs a live Cloudflare run against a reachable trusted relay to satisfy Dreaming definition of done.
- Dream refinement loop progress: generated Dream workflows can invoke `joelclaw.dream.refinement-proposals` as a package-backed `workflow.node.invoke` state selected by the generated machine. The node emits `dream.refinement-proposals.v1` at `dream/refinement-proposals.json`, classifies candidate improvements across kernel memory, package boundaries, workflow-node plugins, schema changes, capture-ingest fixes, capability leases, and mined Dream signals, and feeds the canonical Dream HITL report with actionable reasoning/rating/recommendation proposals plus source refs. Latest live Dream preflight `.wrangler/workflow-app/dream-preflight/latest-dream-preflight.json` is blocked only on relay URL/token/config/healthz gates. Latest blocked run request is `run-live-dream-memory-fabric-20260610T061707360Z-c143439a` with `preflight.refreshed=true`, `submit.attempted=false`, and an explicit live-submit blocker requiring the exact relay-boundary sign-off phrase.
- Dream HITL report progress: `joelclaw.dream.hitl-report` now renders a stronger canonical MDSvX report body: dreams first, no `Candidate review`, report-node/proof/coverage/access/standard sections below, explicit generated-machine D2 state-machine source, and a `What did not happen` section that says the node did not return raw transcripts, publish Wzrrd, or mutate Brain/packages/indexes/policies. The report proof contract now includes `generatedArtifacts.machine`, `generatedArtifacts.harness`, `generatedArtifacts.verificationContract`, planner/plan metadata, generated artifact hashes, and a `stateMachineFigure.sourceKind=generated-xstate-machine` figure derived from the pinned XState config instead of a static Dream node list.
- Capability broker progress: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-capability-lease-broker.ts` implements production-intended `discord.message.send`, `wzrrd.site.publish`, `github.branch.commit`, `github.pull-request.create`, and `linear.comment.create` leases with D1 as the queryable lease/receipt status index and Artifacts as the redacted lease/execution receipt store. It validates actor identity, capability, review policy, trusted secret refs for real side effects, and pinned payload hash before issuing authority. Denied requests do not mutate D1.
- Discord execution progress: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-discord-message-adapter.ts` implements the production-intended Discord API adapter for leased `discord.message.send`. It resolves bot-token material only inside the adapter, blocks hash/resource/review/secret failures before fetch, sends to Discord API v10 with `allowed_mentions.parse: []` and nonce enforcement, and returns redacted delivery results. Dry-run stays on the lease path without materializing secrets or calling Discord. `WorkflowApp` writes typed `workflow.discord-message-approval.v1` artifacts for actors with `discord.send`, points the lease review gate at that artifact, and includes Discord payload/approval/receipt refs in final capture.
- Review gate progress: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-review-gate-actor.ts` implements the production-intended Cloudflare review gate summary adapter. It writes typed `workflow.review-summary.v1` artifacts, persists D1 `review_gates` status as `summary-captured`, mirrors the summary as a D1 `review-summary` receipt row, and is the default front-door review gate when no test adapter is injected.
- Review surface progress: `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-artifacts-review-surface.ts` implements the production-intended Artifact-backed review surface publisher. It writes typed `workflow.review-surface.v1` documents that gather the plan artifact, generated machine, generated harness, verification contract/result, package refs, lane receipts, capability receipts, review summary, event log, output target, redacted artifact refs, `definitionOfDone.workflowChain`, and `definitionOfDone.reconciliation`. The workflow-chain audit marks planner/worker execution captured only when their receipts are real agent lanes; verification is captured by either a real verifier lane or a plan-selected deterministic verifier result. Integration-test/memory lanes and verifier bypasses stay visibly incomplete. Proposal reconciliation now audits package-first primitive, Artifact-backed package pinning, entitlement/trust policy, generated XState workflow, real Pi lanes, capability-leased side effects, receipt-backed review surface, and observability/redaction envelope against configured Wzrrd acceptance refs. `WorkflowRunReceipt` carries `reviewSurfaceArtifact`, so capture has a final review-surface receipt instead of only a summary blob.
- Wzrrd delivery progress: Wzrrd review-surface delivery is now a leased capability, not just `outputTarget.kind`. When the generated plan asks for Wzrrd output, `WorkflowApp` writes `payloads/wzrrd-publish.json` as typed `wzrrd.publish-payload.v1`, requests a `wzrrd.site.publish` lease, executes a Wzrrd publisher adapter, records a Wzrrd capability receipt, and includes the payload/approval/receipt refs in the final run receipt. Dry-run still leases and does not materialize secrets. Real publication now uses `createCloudflareWzrrdPublishAdapter`, which requires an approved non-dry-run lease, trusted Wzrrd publish secret ref, adapter-local `WZRRD_API_TOKEN` materialization, and review-surface hash verification before publishing `index.html` plus `review-surface.json` to Wzrrd's JSON API. `WorkflowApp` only requests the real lease for actors with `wzrrd.publish`, and writes typed `workflow.wzrrd-publish-approval.v1` as the review gate approval ref. The fixed safety envelope admits a review-surface delivery lease loop via `requestingReviewSurfaceDeliveryLease` and `executingReviewSurfaceDelivery`. Live proof: `run-live-wzrrd-publish-20260609T044127Z-900769e2` captured with Wzrrd delivery `published`, dryRun `false`, and public URL `https://run-live-wzrrd-publish-20260609t044127z-900769e2.wzrrd.sh/`.
- GitHub PR delivery progress: GitHub review-surface delivery is now a two-lease path in production `src/app`, not just the old `cloud-capability-lease-broker-spike` receipt. When the generated plan asks for `outputTarget.kind === "github-pr"`, `WorkflowApp` writes `payloads/github-branch-commit.json` as typed `github.branch-commit-payload.v1`, leases `github.branch.commit`, records that capability receipt, then writes `payloads/github-pr.json` as typed `github.pull-request-payload.v1`, leases `github.pull-request.create`, records the PR capability receipt, and includes both payload/approval/receipt chains in the final run receipt. Dry-run still leases both operations and does not materialize a GitHub token. Real branch commit uses `createCloudflareGitHubBranchCommitAdapter`, which requires an approved non-dry-run lease, trusted GitHub branch secret ref, adapter-local token materialization, repository/base/head binding, pinned payload hash verification, per-file content hashes, safe repository paths, and GitHub refs/trees/commits writes. Real PR creation uses `createCloudflareGitHubPullRequestAdapter`, which requires an approved non-dry-run lease, trusted GitHub PR secret ref, adapter-local token materialization, repository/base/head resource binding, and pinned payload hash verification before calling GitHub's create-pull-request API. `WorkflowApp` only exits dry-run for actors with both `github.branch.commit` and `github.pr.create`, and writes typed `workflow.github-branch-commit-approval.v1` plus `workflow.github-pr-approval.v1` review gate artifacts. Live deployed dry-run proof `run-live-github-pr-dryrun-20260609T060703Z-9bba1f11` captured the prior PR-only dry-run path through real Pi planner/worker/verifier lanes on Worker version `97931a7d-8558-4fb8-bef1-89cebe0d80e2`. Live deployed non-dry-run proof `run-live-github-branch-pr-20260609T065340Z-f82a6d90` captured the branch-then-PR path through real Pi planner/worker/verifier lanes on Worker version `1bfc4edd-67e2-461f-b445-ac327a5a3c44`, executed `github.branch.commit`, executed `github.pull-request.create`, committed `2b67364fd7435e64b1916c5a68b768ceb48605ea`, and opened `https://github.com/joelhooks/pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows/pull/16`.
- Linear comment delivery progress: Linear review-surface delivery is now a leased path in production `src/app` with integration and live dry-run proof. When the generated plan asks for `outputTarget.kind === "linear"`, `WorkflowApp` writes `payloads/linear-comment.json` as typed `linear.comment-payload.v1`, leases `linear.comment.create` on `linear.issue:<issueRef>`, records the capability receipt, and includes payload/approval/receipt refs in the final run receipt. Dry-run still leases and does not materialize a Linear token. Real comment creation uses `createCloudflareLinearCommentAdapter`, which requires an approved non-dry-run lease, trusted Linear secret ref, adapter-local token materialization, Linear GraphQL issue lookup by id/key, body hash verification, and pinned payload hash/resource binding before calling `commentCreate`. `WorkflowApp` only exits dry-run for actors with `linear.comment.create`, and writes typed `workflow.linear-comment-approval.v1` as the review gate artifact. Integration tests now cover the adapter, D1 broker persistence, app dry-run path, app approved path, and planner prompt output-target contract. Live deployed dry-run receipt `run-live-linear-dryrun-20260609T072514Z-fee16d9c` captured through Worker version `b6d6794b-3ad9-41cc-baa3-36470709bafa` with real `pi-agent-cli` planner/worker/verifier lanes, final review surface kind `linear`, dry-run `linear.comment.create` on `linear.issue:PIWF-123`, a D1 `linear` receipt row, and `31` structured telemetry rows. Live non-dry-run Linear proof still needs a configured `LINEAR_API_TOKEN` and target issue.
- Observability DoD progress: `workflow.review-surface.v1` now carries a typed `definitionOfDone.observability` requirement. The app emits `workflow.observability-pack.v1` through the required `WorkflowObservabilityRecorderPort`, with `createCloudflareArtifactsObservabilityRecorder` as the production-intended Artifact-backed adapter wired in the Cloudflare front door. The pack is written at `run/observability-pack.json` before verifier execution and injected as verifier evidence. It contains structured high-cardinality log records derived from workflow events, planner/worker lane receipts, capability receipts, artifact refs, redaction-safe ids, D1 status projection evidence, sandbox accounting status/duration metrics when real lane receipts provide them, token/cost accounting status plus aggregate `tokenCount`/`tokenCostEstimate` metrics when lane receipts carry explicit accounting, trace propagation status plus aggregate span counts when lane and capability receipts carry propagated trace context, and structured telemetry sink receipts. `AgentLaneReceipt` now supports optional redacted `tokenCostAccounting` and redacted `WorkflowTraceContext`; production-mode real-agent receipts are invalid without trace context. `CapabilityLeaseRequest`, `CapabilityLease`, and `CapabilityLeaseReceipt` now require redacted `WorkflowTraceContext`; `WorkflowApp` derives deterministic side-effect spans for dynamic Discord steps and review-surface delivery operations, brokers preserve those spans, and the recorder projects capability receipt spans into `workflow.capability.receipt` logs. Local coverage proves traced lease issuance/execution for Discord, Wzrrd, GitHub branch, GitHub PR, and Linear, plus app observability-pack projection. `AgentLaneRuntimeRequest` carries trace context into Pi lanes, the Cloudflare Sandbox Pi adapter exposes it to the subprocess and persists it in the committed receipt, and the recorder projects receipt span IDs into lane structured logs. `WorkflowTelemetrySinkPort` now exists; the deployed front-door proof writes Artifacts JSONL at `run/telemetry/structured-logs.jsonl`, D1 rows in `workflow_telemetry_logs`, and Workers Analytics Engine data points through `createCloudflareAnalyticsEngineWorkflowTelemetrySink`. `createExternalHttpWorkflowTelemetrySink` now adds an optional `external-http-structured-logs` adapter that POSTs a redacted `workflow.external-telemetry-batch.v1` payload with endpoint hashing, bearer-token material scoped inside the adapter, blocked receipts on collector failure, and whitelisted high-cardinality fields only. It is wired from `WORKFLOW_EXTERNAL_TELEMETRY_URL`, `WORKFLOW_EXTERNAL_TELEMETRY_BEARER_TOKEN`, and `WORKFLOW_EXTERNAL_TELEMETRY_SINK_ID`; local integration proves both configured export and blocked collector paths, while the live Worker currently has no external collector URL configured. The status projection now also writes D1 `workflow_events`, the Worker exposes `GET /runs/:runId/events` as a redacted `workflow.event-stream.v1` JSON/SSE/WebSocket observer route, and `GET /runs/:runId/debugger` now returns `workflow.debugger-attach.v1` with read-only JSON/SSE/live-tail/WebSocket transports over those same event receipts. Live proof `run-live-trace-propagation-20260609T091147Z-7fdc512f` on Worker version `00f9f6fd-426c-42f0-9e24-3860aab144f9` captured planner/worker/verifier lane `traceContext`, public URL `https://run-live-trace-propagation-20260609t091147z-7fdc512f.wzrrd.sh/`, D1 `31` telemetry rows with one trace and `31` spans, and observability-pack metrics `tracePropagationStatus=captured`, `traceSpanCount=31`, and `structuredLogSinkStatus=captured`; it predates capability receipt spans. Live proof `run-live-capability-trace-20260609T093229Z-eca60175` on Worker version `5b813670-0b3f-4ec4-8d9f-7a2c6810d3f2` captured real Pi planner/worker/verifier lane traces, public URL `https://run-live-capability-trace-20260609t093229z-eca60175.wzrrd.sh/`, public JSON Discord capability receipt `traceContext`, D1 `31` telemetry rows with one trace and `31` spans, observability-pack `workflow.capability.receipt` log using the Discord capability span, and Artifact receipt proof for post-verifier Wzrrd capability span. Live WebSocket observer proof on Worker version `e1e8229b-6607-4805-a9cd-c5f74aae1956` connected to `wss://pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows.joelhooks.workers.dev/runs/run-live-deterministic-verifier-20260609T110555-870f1138/events?after=19`, replayed event id `20`, sent `workflow.snapshot`, sent typed `workflow.tail.closed` with `reason=terminal-state`, and closed with code `1000`. Live debugger attach proof on Worker version `4495d4c6-a82d-4007-93f6-cc21c4aedbb3` fetched `https://pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows.joelhooks.workers.dev/runs/run-live-deterministic-verifier-20260609T110555-870f1138/debugger?after=19`, returned `workflow.debugger-attach.v1`, `eventCount=20`, `latestEventIndex=20`, `latestStatus=captured`, read-only/no-secret attach policy, and JSON/SSE/live-tail/WebSocket transport URLs. Live proof `run-live-token-cost-accounting-20260609T083009Z-634cb024` remains the token/cost plumbing proof; its observability pack reports `metrics.tokenCostAccountingStatus=not-yet-instrumented`, `metrics.tokenCount=null`, and `metrics.tokenCostEstimate=null` because Pi emitted no numeric usage/cost metadata. Current limitation: live external HTTP collector endpoint/secret configuration, active debugger UI/sandbox control beyond the read-only attach descriptor, and live token/cost capture from Pi/provider usage metadata remain open.
- Live-tail correction: the older observability limitation that listed true live tailing as open is superseded by Worker version `749ae924-c5ed-47df-a772-c86167a7a4be`. `GET /runs/:runId/events?tail=live` now streams from D1 `workflow_events` with resume support and typed `workflow.event-tail-control.v1` close events. Live receipt `run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609T102116Z-e1db65c8` captured with public URL `https://run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609t102116z-e1db65c8.wzrrd.sh/`, public JSON `https://run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609t102116z-e1db65c8.wzrrd.sh/review-surface.json`, event URL `https://pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows.joelhooks.workers.dev/runs/run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609T102116Z-e1db65c8/events`, first live-tail SSE ids `1..5` while `POST /runs` was still in flight, terminal-tail SSE ids `6..20` with `workflow.tail.closed reason=terminal-state`, D1 `workflow_events` rows `20`, D1 telemetry rows `31`, Discord message id `1513851033913393233`, and Wzrrd delivery `published`. WebSocket observer is captured by Worker version `e1e8229b-6607-4805-a9cd-c5f74aae1956`; read-only debugger attach descriptor is captured by Worker version `4495d4c6-a82d-4007-93f6-cc21c4aedbb3`; remaining live-observer gaps are active debugger UI/sandbox control, live configured external HTTP collector proof, and live token/cost capture from Pi/provider metadata. Preceding proof `run-live-event-tail-20260609T101723Z-bfac4bb6` blocked because the prompt asked the in-run verifier to prove an external observer SSE receipt it could not read; observer receipts either remain external proof or must be pinned as verifier evidence before verification.
