Real-scope correction: the memory-backed path is only a Vitest integration contract for schemas, artifacts, and receipts. It belongs in `tests/integration/`, not as app vocabulary or a product mode. The product is not real until a Pi planner lane produces the dynamic workflow blueprint and Pi worker/verifier lanes execute it from pinned Artifacts. The reusable lane concept is agent lane, so future Think-framework lanes should fit the same prompt/transcript/output/receipt contract, but first real completion still requires real Pi planner/worker/verifier lanes. Backing doc: `docs/real-pi-agent-scope.md`.

Deterministic verifier correction: the production app now has a real deterministic verifier port for contracts that select `builtin:artifact-evidence-integrity.v1`. It verifies pinned worker output evidence, evidence hashes, side-effect receipt coverage, and observability-pack presence, blocks unknown semantic checks, and writes a structured `workflow.verification-result.v1` artifact. This satisfies the "Pi verifier lane or deterministic verifier selected by the plan" branch without using memory adapters as fake product execution; the default real planner still selects a Pi verifier lane.

