Primary receipts:

- Pi supports subscription auth via `/login`; tokens live in `~/.pi/agent/auth.json` and auto-refresh. Source: `/Users/joel/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/providers.md`.
- Pi supports single-shot print mode via `runPrintMode` and subprocess RPC via `pi --mode rpc --no-session`. Source: `/Users/joel/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md`.
- Cloudflare Sandbox creates isolated Linux container sandboxes, with per-session/per-task naming and explicit `destroy()` cleanup. Source: `https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/concepts/sandboxes/index.md`.
- Cloudflare Containers pricing is Workers Paid + active container resources: memory/disk provisioned while running, CPU active usage only, plus Workers/Durable Objects/logs/egress. Source: `https://developers.cloudflare.com/containers/pricing/index.md`.
- `just-bash` is an in-process virtual bash with no arbitrary native binary execution; it is useful as a cheap command sandbox/controller, not as the substrate for running the Pi CLI. Source: `vercel-labs/just-bash/packages/just-bash/README.md`.
- Cloudflare Artifacts stores durable, versioned file trees behind Git-compatible repos; repos have scoped tokens, remotes, history, refs, and durable state. Source: `https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/concepts/how-artifacts-works/`.
- Cloudflare's Sandbox SDK + Artifacts example uses the same ID for sandbox and Artifacts repo, passes a short-lived authenticated Git remote into the sandbox, and lets sandbox code use normal `git clone/fetch/pull/push`. Source: `https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/examples/sandbox-sdk-artifacts/`.
